It could be useful to clearly split these into two groups: the ones
whose effect can be gained as an intrinsic (without eating the ring),
and which thus become useless at some point in the game, and the ones
that remain worth carrying around for when you need them.

>  o ring of levitation to float over traps, water, lava, and holes
> (except in Sokoban). Note that levitation prevents several common
> activities and does not prevent water monsters from drowning you.

You'll need _some_ way to cross water, and the =oL is one of the most
convenient ones.  So this is definitely one to keep with you.

>  o ring of invisibility provides temporary invisibility. The hard
> monsters can all "see invisible" so it doesn't help for the mid to end
> game.

A source of temporary invisibility makes it easier to acquire the
permanent intrinsic (as well as see invisible) by eating stalkers;
this may be worth noting.  The same applies to poison resistance, and
to a lesser extent to the other resistances.

Speaking of resistances, I strongly recommend the "Eating Corpses For
Food And Intrinsics" spoiler[1].  Most of the information in it can of
course also be found in the food-343 spoiler, but I find the table
format very useful for answering questions like "should I eat that?"
or, with keyword search, "what should I eat to get this intrinsic?".

[1] http://www.geocities.com/dcorbett42/nethack/corpse.htm

